  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A Carnot engine whose heat sinks at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, has an efficiency of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></math>. By how many degrees should the temperature of the source be changed to increase the efficiency by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the original efficiency ?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AV7VE",
      "text": "Increases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fHGYV",
      "text": "Increases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9EiBf",
      "text": "Increases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eCQa1",
      "text": "Increases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>73</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Efficiency of carnot engine is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>sink</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>source</mi></msub></mfrac></math>.</p><p>For initial case:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>sink</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>273</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>So we can write,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>300</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>Now for the second case:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>sink</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>After increasing the previous efficiency by 100%, value of efficiency will get doubled.</p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>300</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>Increase in temperature required will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
